{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02601",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.61,
      "end_seconds": 8.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.89,
      "end_seconds": 14.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.7,
      "end_seconds": 26.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Well, uh, mainly restlessness. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.34,
      "end_seconds": 32.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.73,
      "end_seconds": 46.35,
      "duration_seconds": 13.62,
      "text": "Iron tablets. I take it once a day for my blood count. I'm supposed to take it regularly, uh, but I don't always manage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.33,
      "end_seconds": 50.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.23,
      "end_seconds": 54.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "It's been going on for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.71,
      "end_seconds": 60.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.57,
      "end_seconds": 81.6,
      "duration_seconds": 17.03,
      "text": "Mild, really. Oh, and impatience. That's been about the same, three days. Um, as for impatience, about a four out of ten. I've also had difficulty concentrating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.69,
      "end_seconds": 88.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Have you noticed head injury, low mood, thoughts of self-harm or drug use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.22,
      "end_seconds": 98.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "I haven't had head injury, low mood, thoughts of self-harm or drug use, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.4,
      "end_seconds": 103.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.31,
      "end_seconds": 108.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Mm, no, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.85,
      "end_seconds": 111.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.65,
      "end_seconds": 114.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.59,
      "end_seconds": 122.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "Right, has anyone ever diagnosed you with something? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.27,
      "end_seconds": 146.6,
      "duration_seconds": 23.33,
      "text": "I've, I've had depression for about a year now. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I mean, I have low haemoglobin, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.61,
      "end_seconds": 156.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Okay, I can see depression in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.44,
      "end_seconds": 169.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Okay, now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.21,
      "end_seconds": 185.98,
      "duration_seconds": 12.77,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. No, I share a house with my brother. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.05,
      "end_seconds": 194.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.65,
      "end_seconds": 197.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Milk, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 199.11,
      "end_seconds": 208.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Heart rate 86, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, respiratory rate 17, BP is 123 over 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.92,
      "end_seconds": 210.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.21,
      "end_seconds": 215.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.74,
      "end_seconds": 220.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.25,
      "end_seconds": 236.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Your pulse and blood pressure are normal and your examination is unremarkable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.12,
      "end_seconds": 243.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.47,
      "end_seconds": 263.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.44,
      "text": "Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with possible adult attention deficit disorder at this stage. Thyroid problems is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.78,
      "end_seconds": 269.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.19,
      "end_seconds": 280.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's possible adult attention deficit disorder, and we'll know more once the a questionnaire is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.72,
      "end_seconds": 314.59,
      "duration_seconds": 25.87,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a questionnaire for attention problems. I'm sending you for a thyroid test because of poor concentration. Use lists and reminders while we arrange the specialist assessment. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Let's plan a check after the assessment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.07,
      "end_seconds": 319.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.06,
      "end_seconds": 325.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.22,
      "end_seconds": 329.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}